00:03:32.168 --> 00:03:33.626
It's like... you know what I'm saying?

00:03:33.626 --> 00:03:34.626
You're just like.. you're like,

00:03:34.626 --> 00:03:35.459
"Oh, it's..."

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:38.477
'Cause it ends up being
sometimes about everybody else

00:03:38.477 --> 00:03:39.658
rather than the bride and groom.

00:03:39.658 --> 00:03:40.491
- Exactly.

00:03:40.491 --> 00:03:42.829
And we just wanted our closest
people together to celebrate,

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:44.418
you know, this beautiful thing that,

00:03:44.418 --> 00:03:47.229
again, we never thought
was gonna come about.

00:03:47.229 --> 00:03:49.250
All right. Well, is there any...

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.083
- Room for one more? (clear throat)

00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:50.916
(audience laughing)

00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:51.749
- Yes. Room for one.

00:03:51.749 --> 00:03:52.597
He's hanging out and...

00:03:52.597 --> 00:03:56.001
Wait, are there any
cool things in Scotland?

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:57.098
Do they have like wedding things?

00:03:57.098 --> 00:03:57.931
Like any kind of cool wedding?

00:03:57.931 --> 00:03:59.486
- So, we're gonna do a mini
Highlands game with the guests.

00:03:59.486 --> 00:04:00.361
- Oh, mini Highland games.

00:04:00.361 --> 00:04:01.194
That's amazing.

00:04:01.194 --> 00:04:02.027
- Wait, what?

00:04:02.027 --> 00:04:02.860
- Which should be fun.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.693
I don't really know what that entails

00:04:03.693 --> 00:04:04.538
but he keeps saying, "Mini Highland."

00:04:04.538 --> 00:04:05.371
I'm like, "Yeah," like (indistinct)

00:04:05.371 --> 00:04:06.439
- Like archery like things or like...

00:04:06.439 --> 00:04:07.598
- Oh, not archery.

00:04:07.598 --> 00:04:08.431
- Oh, well.

00:04:08.431 --> 00:04:09.264
- We don't have archery.

00:04:09.264 --> 00:04:10.305
We throw capers.

00:04:10.305 --> 00:04:13.387
We toss tree trunks and
lob rocks around and...

00:04:13.387 --> 00:04:15.032
- You thought archery was weird.

00:04:15.032 --> 00:04:16.615
And then you said? (laughs)

00:04:16.615 --> 00:04:17.913
- Throwing tree trunks.

00:04:17.913 --> 00:04:18.746
You wanna come?

00:04:18.746 --> 00:04:19.579
Let's do it. You're excited.

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:20.412
- I'll throw a tree-

00:04:20.412 --> 00:04:21.245
- Are you having a caly?

00:04:21.245 --> 00:04:22.078
- Yes. We're gonna do...

00:04:22.078 --> 00:04:23.426
We're like the whole,
like, I want like the tree.

00:04:23.426 --> 00:04:24.884
They're gonna wear kilts.

00:04:24.884 --> 00:04:25.786
- It's some madness.

00:04:25.786 --> 00:04:27.244
It's organized madness.

00:04:27.244 --> 00:04:29.916
It's dancing, but everyone
dances and they very organized.

00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:32.999
But it literally gets faster
and faster and it's chaos.

00:04:32.999 --> 00:04:33.918
It's chaos, organized chaos.

00:04:33.918 --> 00:04:34.751
It's brilliant.

00:04:34.751 --> 00:04:35.584
- This sounds fun.

00:04:35.584 --> 00:04:36.417
- Can't wait.
- Yeah.

00:04:36.417 --> 00:04:38.418
- Yeah. That sounds way better
than weddings over here.

00:04:38.418 --> 00:04:40.656
- Yeah. I mean, and you know,

00:04:40.656 --> 00:04:41.988
the baby's gonna wear kilt.

00:04:41.988 --> 00:04:43.233
My son Jace, he's gonna wear...

00:04:43.233 --> 00:04:44.646
So, it's gonna be real cute.

00:04:44.646 --> 00:04:46.269
- Oh my gosh. I love it.

00:04:46.269 --> 00:04:47.102
All right.

00:04:47.102 --> 00:04:47.935
(audience applauds)

00:04:47.935 --> 00:04:52.634
So, I mean, I feel like we've
had kind of similar worlds.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:54.377
I feel like we've had like similar things

00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:56.755
kind of happen with us in recent years.

00:04:56.755 --> 00:04:59.126
And so to write a book,
first of all, is so brave.

00:04:59.126 --> 00:05:01.799
I mean, I wrote songs to get my stuff out

00:05:01.799 --> 00:05:05.127
but like post-divorce, like,
writing a book that, like,

00:05:05.127 --> 00:05:08.167
that's hard to be that
vulnerable after something, like,

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.999
so tragic in your own life.

00:05:09.999 --> 00:05:11.237
Like how was that?

00:05:11.237 --> 00:05:12.176
- It was really hard.

00:05:12.176 --> 00:05:14.097
And you know, my ex and I we wrote a book

00:05:14.097 --> 00:05:16.375
after the infidelity in our marriage

00:05:16.375 --> 00:05:18.317
and how we got through that.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:21.626
And we actually had another
book deal about trust.

00:05:21.626 --> 00:05:23.222
And that's when I found
out about more things.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:26.805
I think, you know, once I
kind of rose up from all that,

00:05:26.805 --> 00:05:28.279
it was, I needed to write this book

00:05:28.279 --> 00:05:30.428
about trusting myself and moving on.

00:05:30.428 --> 00:05:31.987
And this book is...

00:05:31.987 --> 00:05:35.857
it's truly about my journey
and looking in the mirror.

00:05:35.857 --> 00:05:37.175
'Cause I realized, I was like,

00:05:37.175 --> 00:05:39.005
"Okay," when I started
the book I was very angry.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.279
I was bitter, I was angry.

00:05:40.279 --> 00:05:41.728
- For a good reason.
- I was mad.

00:05:41.728 --> 00:05:44.335
And then I realized that I had
to kind of look in the mirror

00:05:44.335 --> 00:05:46.807
and go, "Okay, there's a lot
of pieces that I contributed."

00:05:46.807 --> 00:05:48.817
I had a lot of brokenness
even before I met him.

00:05:48.817 --> 00:05:51.609
So I had to fix these,
whatever this brokenness is

00:05:51.609 --> 00:05:53.904
to not repeat the same toxic patterns

00:05:53.904 --> 00:05:55.945
that I was bringing to it as well.

00:05:55.945 --> 00:05:58.124
- Which is so helpful
for anyone going through.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.472
'Cause I don't think people realize too

00:05:59.472 --> 00:06:01.279
when you go through like
a divorce, it's loss.

00:06:01.279 --> 00:06:02.207
It's like grief.

00:06:02.207 --> 00:06:05.826
I had never experienced
anything quite like that.

00:06:05.826 --> 00:06:08.108
- Well, your world is taken away from you.

00:06:08.108 --> 00:06:08.941
- Yeah.

00:06:08.941 --> 00:06:10.407
- The world that you
imagined for your children.

00:06:10.407 --> 00:06:12.325
And that's not a world
that I wanted for my kids.

00:06:12.325 --> 00:06:15.897
And so I had to go, "Okay,
how do I now single parent,

00:06:15.897 --> 00:06:16.857
"how do I walk through this,

00:06:16.857 --> 00:06:19.148
"how do I walk through despising this man

00:06:19.148 --> 00:06:20.487
"that ruined my life?"

00:06:20.487 --> 00:06:23.148
But then realizing now
it was the greatest thing

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:24.039
that ever happened to me,

00:06:24.039 --> 00:06:27.041
knowing that like, I finally
fell in love with myself

00:06:27.041 --> 00:06:27.930
for the process.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.345
- Because that is the hardest part,

00:06:29.345 --> 00:06:30.803
because I think the
thing that I went through

00:06:30.803 --> 00:06:32.316
and I find that you did as well,

00:06:32.316 --> 00:06:36.810
like, via talking about trust
and what this book is about,

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.600
literally, it's you're not...

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.785
Like the fact that when you
wake up one day and you go,

00:06:40.785 --> 00:06:43.975
"I cannot trust my
decision making skills,"

00:06:43.975 --> 00:06:46.044
like, "There is something wrong with me."

00:06:46.044 --> 00:06:48.693
Like, I'm like, "'Cause I
made a decision to do this,

00:06:48.693 --> 00:06:51.023
"and I made a decision to do that."

00:06:51.023 --> 00:06:53.685
That's the messed up part is in therapy,

00:06:53.685 --> 00:06:55.484
is when you learn, you're like,

00:06:55.484 --> 00:06:57.524
"I'm having a hard time just trusting me,

00:06:57.524 --> 00:06:59.044
"like, let alone someone else."

00:06:59.044 --> 00:07:00.254
- And I think there was that piece.

00:07:00.254 --> 00:07:02.593
And then also like, I
did not respect myself.

00:07:02.593 --> 00:07:03.663
I didn't love myself.

00:07:03.663 --> 00:07:06.533
And so why would I expect
that from someone else?

00:07:06.533 --> 00:07:07.960
He could never have given that to me.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.131
- Or how do you know how to receive it

00:07:09.131 --> 00:07:10.170
if you don't know how
to give it to yourself?

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:11.003
- 1000%. Yeah.

00:07:11.003 --> 00:07:11.836
- Yeah. It's a very-

00:07:11.836 --> 00:07:13.256
- Writing the book also must have been

00:07:13.256 --> 00:07:14.707
like a process of therapy as well, right?

00:07:14.707 --> 00:07:15.747
- Oh, it was, yeah.

00:07:15.747 --> 00:07:18.565
And just doing, you know, the hard work

00:07:18.565 --> 00:07:20.115
and really digging deep and go,

00:07:20.115 --> 00:07:22.215
"Okay, what are all the
messages that I've believed

00:07:22.215 --> 00:07:24.298
for the last 30 plus years of my life

00:07:24.298 --> 00:07:25.688
that I have to now retrain my brain that,

00:07:25.688 --> 00:07:26.997
"Oh, wait a minute, I don't deserve that

00:07:26.997 --> 00:07:28.179
"and I do deserve respect."

00:07:28.179 --> 00:07:29.739
In this new relationship, everyone's like,

00:07:29.739 --> 00:07:31.118
"Well, why is it different?"

00:07:31.118 --> 00:07:32.099
I'm like, "He respects me

00:07:32.099 --> 00:07:34.270
"but it's because I now
know I deserve respect."

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.049
- Yeah. Oh my gosh. Yes.

00:07:36.049 --> 00:07:38.216
- Now, you know, I'm so
thankful for the relationship

00:07:38.216 --> 00:07:39.424
that I do have with my ex now.

00:07:39.424 --> 00:07:41.179
We have a great co-parenting situation

00:07:41.179 --> 00:07:42.170
and we've really...
- That's amazing.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:43.598
- ... formed a new relationship,

00:07:43.598 --> 00:07:45.011
but we had to let go of the resentment,

00:07:45.011 --> 00:07:46.876
'cause we both had
resentment from the marriage.

00:07:46.876 --> 00:07:48.731
And so it was able to go,

00:07:48.731 --> 00:07:50.700
"Okay, now this is our new relationship,"

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.571
and moving forward.

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:54.691
- And that's not easy to do.
- No, it's not.

00:07:54.691 --> 00:07:55.575
But we love our kids.

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:56.903
- That's what I'm saying.

00:07:56.903 --> 00:07:59.483
It's the kids that really
changes that, I feel,

00:07:59.483 --> 00:08:00.316
'cause you'll do anything for them.

00:08:00.316 --> 00:08:02.681
Have you ever had a moment like
that when you figured out...

00:08:02.681 --> 00:08:03.721
You went through something rough

00:08:03.721 --> 00:08:04.927
and you figured out
something about yourself

00:08:04.927 --> 00:08:06.122
that you didn't know?

00:08:06.122 --> 00:08:07.671
- I don't know. I think time does that,

00:08:07.671 --> 00:08:08.641
and age as well, right.

00:08:08.641 --> 00:08:11.462
And I guess even now I'm
kind of going through that,

00:08:11.462 --> 00:08:12.964
you know, I'm in the 40 club.

00:08:12.964 --> 00:08:16.364
And yeah, you get a lot
the time to like reflect

00:08:16.364 --> 00:08:20.624
and I'm also coming to the
end of a journey of my acting

00:08:20.624 --> 00:08:22.122
in a certain show that I'm doing.

00:08:22.122 --> 00:08:25.224
So yeah, I guess I'm
always reflecting on that.

00:08:25.224 --> 00:08:27.174
But I guess, acting is almost my therapy,

00:08:27.174 --> 00:08:30.263
you know, writing books is
also another way of doing it.

00:08:30.263 --> 00:08:31.355
- And it's, you know,

00:08:31.355 --> 00:08:33.953
we've all been told messages
from our childhood trauma

00:08:33.953 --> 00:08:35.843
or past or from past relationships

00:08:35.843 --> 00:08:38.283
and you know, not letting
that be the truth.

00:08:38.283 --> 00:08:41.115
And so knowing what is the
truth and trusting that

00:08:41.115 --> 00:08:42.403
and it's hard,

00:08:42.403 --> 00:08:44.155
sometimes old messages still come up like,

00:08:44.155 --> 00:08:45.104
"Oh, maybe I'm not good enough."

00:08:45.104 --> 00:08:46.854
It's like, no, those are old messages.

00:08:46.854 --> 00:08:49.084
What's the new and what's true?

00:08:49.084 --> 00:08:51.974
- Yeah. Oh, it's gonna be
the most helpful book ever

00:08:51.974 --> 00:08:53.821
for so many people, including me.

00:08:53.821 --> 00:08:55.278
I'll be reading it.

00:08:55.278 --> 00:08:57.616
